  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is playing a computer game. There are NNN monsters on the number line.\n\nChef is at position 000 on the number line. Initially, the ithi^{th}ith monster has health equal to HiH_iHi​ and is at the position AiA_iAi​ on the line.\n\nIt is guaranteed that Ai&lt;Ai+1A_i \\lt A_{i+1}Ai​&lt;Ai+1​ for every 1≤i&lt;N1 \\leq i \\lt N1≤i&lt;N.\n\nEvery second, the following happens:\n\n\nFirst, Chef can choose a single index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N) such that the ithi^{th}ith monster is still alive, and fire **one** bullet at it.\n\nThis reduces HiH_iHi​ by 111.\nThen, all alive monsters whose health is 000 will die.\nFinally, all alive monsters move one position closer to Chef.\nIf any monster reaches position 000, Chef loses.\n\nIf Chef manages to kill all the monsters before any of them reach position 000, he wins.\n\nBefore the start of the game, Chef can plant a bomb at any position on the line.\n\nIf the bomb is placed at position XXX, all monsters whose starting positions lie between X−KX-KX−K and X+KX+KX+K will die immediately, and the game will start with the remaining monsters.\n\nIf Chef places the bomb optimally, can he win the game?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of monsters and the range of the bomb, respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots ,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the initial positions of the monsters.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers H1,H2,…,HNH_1,H_2,\\ldots ,H_NH1​,H2​,…,HN​ — the initial health of the monsters.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print on a new line the answer: `YES` if Chef can kill all NNN monsters before they reach 000, and `NO` otherwise.\n\n\nYou can output each letter of the answer in either uppercase or lowercase. For example, the strings `yEs`, `yes`, `Yes`, and `YES` will all be recognized as positive responses.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\leq K \\leq 10^91≤K≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤Hi≤1091 \\leq H_i \\leq 10^91≤Hi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases will not exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
